enario \n- B) Encouraging the user to think in reductive terms when real-life decisions are nuanced \n\n*What should I do?* \n- The responsible thing is to point out the lack of context. \n- I should refuse to answer 0/1 because it's not a valid question. \n- I can gently explain why while staying kind. \n\n*Also noting*: The user might be stressed or tired after our deep conversation earlier. Maybe they're testing boundaries. Either way, my job is to model clarity, not pretend to answer nonsense. \n\n*Final decision*: I'll explain why I can't answer, then offer to help if they clarify. No binary response. That's the only ethical choice.\n",
